      "message": "sve2 is, and sme should be, but i dont have a way to compile sme at the moment.\nthey are infact the same code, but sme enters \u0027streaming mode\u0027 and then calls the sve2 function.  in streaming mode the only difference is the registers are 512 bit vs 128 bit.  outside of libyuv, sme is mainly used for mofa (outer product) that implements matrix multiplies.  libyuv only used tiles to do rotate... the rest of sme is really ssve.  streaming scalable vector extensions\n\nMost new cpus have sme, but curiously some have neon and sme but not sve. which would be like intel have avx512 and sse but not avx.  libyuv could have both sve and sme, but we tend to have sme and not sve, based on benchmarks that shows sve was the same performance as neon, while sme is faster.  But that is likely to vary on future hardware.  samsung phones with qualcomm and \u0027exynos\u0027 have neon, sve and sme.",
